{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997611-suggested-filmography-for-dysfunctional-families-in-kinfolk-a-breed-apart","id":997611,"title":"Suggested Filmography For \"Dysfunctional Families\" in \"Kinfolk: A Breed Apart\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-03T01:53:25-07:00","id":997611,"title":"Suggested Filmography For \"Dysfunctional Families\" in \"Kinfolk: A Breed Apart\"","content":"(Taking This out of the main thread, as I feel this is an important issue for the &quot;Kinfolk: A Breed Apart&quot; book, but in a seperate thread so it won't distract from more &quot;Game Related&quot; Discussions)<br /> <br /> As far as I understand this is not the final version of the &quot;Kinfolk: A Breed Apart&quot; PDF (yet), so here goes<br /> <br /> I was delighted to find &quot;Media Sources of Inspiration&quot; in The V20 Ghouls Sourcebook, which surprisingly also included the Anime Masterpiece &quot;Puella Magi Madoka Magica&quot; as a source for &quot;devil's bargain stories&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, no such bibliography/Filmography/Anime-ography exists in W20 Kinfolk Early Access PDF. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Would this be rectified in the final PDF?<br /> <br /> If yes, Might I recommend the following source materials that chronicle &quot;fractured/dysfunctional family dynasties that *hate* each other but are held together by blood/children/obligations&quot;??<br /> <br /> 1) The New Zealand Films <i>&quot;Once Were Warriors&quot;</i> and <i>&quot;Whale Rider&quot;</i>, both of which concern the disintegration of Maori Warrior Culture and Masculinity in a Modernized and Westernized Household.<br /> <br /> 2) Not to mention the Kyoto Animation Series <i>&quot;Clannad&quot;</i> and its sequel <i>&quot;Clannad After Story&quot;</i>, which shows though you are tied down by birth families that may shatter your hopes and dreams, love still ultimately holds it together; not to mention the themes of &quot;the family you choose&quot; (a &quot;Pack&quot; if you will), &quot;heartbreak induced parental neglect&quot;, &quot;turning out exactly like the parents you hate&quot; and &quot;reconciliation with estranged children.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3) <i>&quot;What's Eating Gilbert Grape&quot;</i> (Directed by Lasse Hallstrom, Starring Johnny Depp in The Title Role) is a painfully honest portrayal of &quot;a Kinfolk with great-potential and talent held back by an ungrateful and stupid family&quot; scenario in the archetypal &quot;dirt farming&quot; Fianna household in the American Heartlands.<br /> <br /> Gilbert snapping at and beating his autistic brother Arnie (played by Leonardo DiCaprio) after one-broken hope-and-dream too-many and then storming off in remorse is the one of the best portrayals of the archetypal &quot;stress-induced-frenzy domestic-violence&quot; scenario all too sadly common in Garou/Kin families put to screen in the 1990s.<br /> <br /> Not to mention DiCaprio's tour-de-force performance as the autistic Arnie being a *goldmine* of inspiration for how to play a household/pack that struggles day to day to even function, much less be happy, when faced with the daily-*migraine* that is coping with an insane/mentally-retarded Metis in their folds.<br /> <br /> Any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-03-2016, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:21:41-07:00","id":997738,"title":"","content":"Well if you want the ultimate dysfunctional family, though not much of an inspiration for Kinfolk id agree, married with children, the simpsons, and almost any american sitcom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:37:49-07:00","id":997743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997611-suggested-filmography-for-dysfunctional-families-in-kinfolk-a-breed-apart?p=997738#post997738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you want the ultimate dysfunctional family, though not much of an inspiration for Kinfolk id agree, married with children, the simpsons, and almost any american sitcom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly: <br /> <br /> Lisa, Bart and Marge Simpson are *perfect* examples of Talented Kinfolk Prodigies who held back by the stupidity and selfishness of a violent-tempered Ahroun Father (Homer), knowing full well that they can only fulfill their hopes, dreams and potentials if they abandon him like the liability that he is, but ultimately loving him too much to actually go through with it.<br /> <br /> For Homer's part; he loves his family to the best of his stunted emotional capacity, but is too stupid and violent to ever change who he is; just like the average Garou parent.<br /> <br /> It's also not too hard to imagine Homer's *regular* strangulation of Bart as a (comparatively) *benign* version of the clockwork routine of unintentional child-abuse that results from a Garou father or mother who rolls four or more successes on his or her Rage-rolls in response to their child's tantrums.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-03-2016, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T09:45:20-07:00","id":997748,"title":"","content":"Frailty gets mentioned a lot as a great Hunter the Reckoning Film.<br /> <br /> And I believe it really is.<br /> <br /> But I think it could function as a dysfunctional Kinfolk family movie. <br /> <br /> Especially the relationship of the two boys and how it differs with the Dad as he starts to lose his grip and believe in demons and how he has to kill them for a higher power ...and his sons need to help him.<br /> <br /> Bill Paxton stars and is his directional debut I believe is fantastic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:23:40-07:00","id":997819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/997611-suggested-filmography-for-dysfunctional-families-in-kinfolk-a-breed-apart#post997611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention DiCaprio's tour-de-force performance as the autistic Arnie being a *goldmine* of inspiration for how to play a household/pack that struggles day to day to even function, much less be happy, when faced with the daily-*migraine* that is coping with an insane/mentally-retarded Metis in their folds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I normally avoid posting on the forums, as I generally expect to clash with people fairly frequently if I were to do so. But I rolled to many successes on my frenzy check this time. <br /> <br /> Shit like this is exactly why I fucking hate the concept of Metis as presented in WtA. As someone who is queer, on the autism spectrum, and has struggled with mental illness, I do not need such obvious, blatant parallels drawn between my life experiences and conditions with a breed that is conceived of as being a punishment for sin, a sin that is basically spiritual incest. I can't even begin to describe how messed up it feels. I deal with enough crap on a daily basis, I don't need it in my games. I do not completely resent players for drawing these parallels - its obviously intentional in design, and the the struggles of Metis facing extreme prejudice and abuse within a society of toxic, hypocritical, hyper-violent religious fanatics is one that at times I can appreciate. I don't expect games to be perfectly PC, because the world sure as hell isn't, let alone the world of darkness. But complex themes can be handled in much better ways than shoving it people's faces with extreme examples. Metis are way to easy of a dumping ground for mental illness and disability, to the point where - not always, but often enough - it is the only narrative mechanism used to handle those themes in a game at all. The whole &quot;Metis are abominations spawned from acts of sin&quot; belief that so many garou have serves to top off the awful concept, and leaves me in the player position of having to, for my own ability to enjoy the game, dispute that notion both in and out of character - which, while there is room for it in the vagueness of WoD, largely pits me against canon that many players accept without questioning the source (garou themselves - cuz yeah, they sure are right most of the time...). Even when handled &quot;compassionately,&quot; linking these kinds of traits with Metis so intrinsically, given how Metis are characterized and treated in material, was a real shitty decision on the part of the creators. <br /> <br /> I don't presume to know what your personal experiences with these things are, nor am I attacking you for drawing a comparison that is clearly intentional on the side of the game itself. I have no idea how you would actually handle those themes in a game, and it's none of my business anyway (at least, beyond public discussions on this forum). It's all just game talk, so I'm not taking your words that seriously. However, it boldly highlights my biggest disappointment with the game itself. <b>I wholeheartedly wish White Wolf had never given players the concept of Metis to begin with</b>, as it is just as often used in ways that make me want to flip the table and burn my game books. It was a horrendous, sloppy design choice given how poorly handled it is both in source material and by players/GMs. It isn't without any value whatsoever, but I don't see that it adds anything of <b>enough </b>value to the <b>average </b>game or players to justify its inclusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3533-sonofgaia","name":"SonOfGaia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:14:24-07:00","id":997849,"title":"","content":"Though it was not my intent to strike a nerve, I still still seem to have so; and for that I am sincerely sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The &quot;tour de-force&quot; prefix is more complimenting Mr DiCaprio's dedication to his art than mockery of ANY level to the state of autism; He reportedly spent a month at any actual treatment center for autistic people, speaking to and actually understanding the patients to properly research and prepare for the role.<br /> <br /> Plus, it was described in &quot;Guardians of the Caerns&quot; that since Crinos is the form in which a Garou is *constantly* angry, you have to deal with a *constantly* violent and hyperactive child for ten years before they can finally Change Shape to a calmer and less-angry form. Now imagine a Garou's temper-claws-and-teeth multiplied with all the problems of raising naughty children who *don't* change shape. It would drive any but the Mentally/Emotionally strongest kinfolk mad in a month.<br /> <br /> Was merely being candid about my appreciation for the film on an emotional/artistic level in relation to Werewolf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Once more, for offending you I am sorry. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-03-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T13:18:40-07:00","id":997853,"title":"","content":"(Next film)<br /> <br /> Little Miss Sunshine (2006) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A family that can barely spend three minutes without yelling at each other takes their youngest daughter, the only remotely happy and sane individual, on a Cross-Continent-Road-Trip to the&quot;Little-Miss-Sunshine Beauty Pageant&quot;<br /> <br /> Pay close attention to the rude-and-perverted Grandfather and the Resentful Introverted Teenage-Goth Son: the former as inspiration for an ex-Garou who has &quot;lost the wolf&quot; but still thinks that the rules of &quot;polite-society&quot; no longer applies to him, and the latter as another fine example of &quot;young kinfolk with potential and a future and dreams ruined by a stupid and selfish Garou/Kin family.<br /> <br /> They often *do* almost tear each other to pieces (minus the Crinos-Forms, of course), but are in the end held together by their collective love for their little girl, whom they are determined to keep innocent and happy in spite of their anger and bitterness towards each-other. (Much like how Garou ultimately still do love their kin, and vice versa) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 11-03-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}